course: dictionary
lesson: 111
title: Admiration: respect and pleasure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Admiration is a feeling of liking and respect for someone because they are good, brave or skilful. It can also mean pleasure in looking at something beautiful. Read the clues around the word to tell which meaning is meant.
explain: «Copying someone's clothes or style is often a sign of admiration.» You copy someone because you respect them and want to be like them. So admiration is a feeling, and people show it through what they do.
explain: In a story, Toad imagines «praise and admiration at the recital of his adventures», and then he «began to skip up and down and shout and sing». He is so pleased by the thought of being admired that he cannot keep still. Look for what causes the feeling and how a character behaves.
fact: Admiration is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «some admiration», not «an admiration».
fact: Admiration means a feeling of liking and respect for someone who is good, brave or skilful.
fact: Useful phrases: «full of admiration», «in admiration», «admiration for» someone, and «win the admiration of» someone.
fact: A quick check: swap in the word «respect» or «liking». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Admiration can also mean pleasure in looking at something beautiful, like a painting or a sunset.
exercise: «The crowd watched the gymnast with admiration.» What does admiration mean here? | Boredom with the show | Fear that she might fall | *Respect and liking for her skill | Anger at her for being late
exercise: «Mia looked at the sunset in ___ and said nothing.» Which word fills the gap? | hurry | anger | *admiration | silence
exercise: Toad imagines «praise and admiration at the recital of his adventures». What does recital mean here? | A quiet sleep | A kind of dance | *Telling, as in reading out or retelling | A type of boat
test: Admiration is which kind of word? | Verb | Adverb | Adjective | *Noun
test: Which phrase is in the entry for admiration? | win the race with | *win the admiration of | full of hunger | in a hurry of
exam: Which sentence uses admiration correctly? | The admiration was very sleepy and tall. | The admiration ran quickly down the hill. | She admiration three apples at lunch. | *The fans showed their admiration for the young pianist.
